Hey @jeremysamuel13 @ItsWendell @nathanl — I've added Amazon Bedrock support to my plugin [opencode-anthropic-context-1m](https://github.com/DusKing1/opencode-anthropic-context-1m). It now injects `anthropicBeta: ["context-1m-2025-08-07"]` via the `chat.params` hook for Bedrock, in addition to the existing Anthropic direct API support.

Published as `1.0.1-dev.0` on the `dev` tag — would appreciate if any Bedrock users could help test it.

**Install:**
```jsonc
{
  "plugin": ["opencode-anthropic-context-1m@dev"],
  "provider": {
    "amazon-bedrock": {
      "models": {
        "anthropic.claude-opus-4-6-v1": {
          "limit": { "context": 1000000, "output": 128000 }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

The `plugin` entry handles the beta flag injection automatically. The `models` override bumps the context limit so OpenCode's auto-compaction triggers at ~968K instead of ~168K. No region prefix needed — OpenCode adds it based on your `AWS_REGION`.

Feedback welcome at https://github.com/DusKing1/opencode-anthropic-context-1m/issues

